<title>UK: Bayerhypo sets $100 million December 1999 bond.</title>
<headline>Bayerhypo sets $100 million December 1999 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers  Banque Generale du Luxembourg and Citibank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BAYERISCHE HYPOTHEKEN- UND WECHSEL-BANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    $100 MLN	COUPON     6.125     MATURITY    13.DEC.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.915   PAY DATE  F-17.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.715    SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> YIELD	5.77 PCT</p>
<p> NOTES    F-FIRST SHORT COUPON.</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10	SALE LIMITS US/UK/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 MGT/UND    0.175     SELL CONC  1.20</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND = NOVEMBER 1999 U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
